+### Compound Format
+
+Use `compound: true` to break a duration into several units, largest first:
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h 30m"
+ms(90061000, { compound: true })      // "1d 1h 1m 1s"
+ms(3605000, { compound: true })       // "1h 5s"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h 30m"
+```
+
+- Parts are separated by a space and zero parts are skipped.
+- Days are the largest unit (no weeks, months or years): `400d`, not `1y 35d`.
+- Seconds are the smallest unit. Leftover milliseconds are dropped, so values under one second give `"0s"`.
+- Negative values get a single leading `-`, unless the result is `"0s"`.
+- `compound` takes precedence over `long`.
+
 ### Input Formats (Units)
 
